review_comment:
Don’t fall back to configuring an arbitrary controller when a HomeKit model UID is known but that UID isn’t discoverable. In confirm, if _discovered_controller_uid is set and the subsequent discovery doesn’t return that UID, choosing next(iter(controllers.values())) can set up the wrong controller; instead abort (e.g., no_devices_found/cannot_connect) or require discovery of the specific UID.
```suggestion
            if self._discovered_controller_uid:
                controller = controllers.get(self._discovered_controller_uid)
                if controller is None:
                    _LOGGER.debug(
                        "Discovered controller UID %s was not found during confirmation",
                        self._discovered_controller_uid,
                    )
                    return self.async_abort(reason="no_devices_found")
            else:
                controller = next(iter(controllers.values()))
```

Avoid stopping the shared discovery service on setup failure if other iZone entries are already loaded (or if this call didn’t start the service). As written, a failure to forward setups for one entry will call async_stop_discovery_service() unconditionally, which can break controller updates for other already-loaded entries that rely on the shared discovery listener; track whether the service was newly started and/or check for other loaded entries before stopping it.
```suggestion
    had_loaded_entries = any(
        config_entry.state is config_entries.ConfigEntryState.LOADED
        for config_entry in hass.config_entries.async_entries(IZONE)
    )
    await async_start_discovery_service(hass)
    try:
        await hass.config_entries.async_forward_entry_setups(entry, PLATFORMS)
    except Exception:
        if not had_loaded_entries:
            await async_stop_discovery_service(hass)
```

Avoid prompting for controller selection during SOURCE_IMPORT; if multiple controllers are discovered during YAML import, handle it non-interactively (e.g., create entries for all discovered controllers or deterministically pick one and log).
```suggestion
        import_data = import_data or {}

        if host := import_data.get(CONF_HOST):
            if not (uid := await _async_get_controller_uid(self.hass, host)):
                return self.async_abort(reason="cannot_connect")

            await self.async_set_unique_id(uid)
            self._abort_if_unique_id_configured(updates={CONF_HOST: host})
            return self.async_create_entry(
                title=f"iZone {uid}", data={CONF_HOST: host}
            )

        controllers = await _async_discover_controllers(self.hass)
        if not controllers:
            _LOGGER.debug("No controllers found during import")
            return self.async_abort(reason="no_devices_found")

        unconfigured_controllers = self._async_get_unconfigured_controllers(controllers)
        if not unconfigured_controllers:
            return self.async_abort(reason="already_configured")

        controller = min(
            unconfigured_controllers.values(),
            key=lambda discovered_controller: (
                discovered_controller.device_uid,
                discovered_controller.device_ip,
            ),
        )
        if len(unconfigured_controllers) > 1:
            _LOGGER.info(
                "Multiple iZone controllers discovered during YAML import; "
                "selecting controller %s at %s deterministically",
                controller.device_uid,
                controller.device_ip,
            )

        return await self._async_create_controller_entry(controller)
```

