We can optimize this pattern a bit. :)

`media_title` construction introduces a trailing space when only audio is playing (`f"audio: ... "`). This makes the title inconsistent and forces tests to assert on whitespace. Consider building the title from a list of parts and joining them so there’s no trailing whitespace.
```suggestion
        if self.state != MediaPlayerState.PLAYING:
            return None

        parts: list[str] = []

        if self._playing_audio:
            parts.append(f"audio: {self._receiver.audio_information}")

        if self._playing_video:
            parts.append(f"video: {self._receiver.video_information}")

        if not parts:
            return None

        return " ".join(parts)
```

