review_comment:
`_fetch_node_data` now calls additional endpoints (`version.get()` and `apt.update.get()`). Any `ResourceException` raised by these calls will currently be caught in `_async_update_data` and re-raised as `no_nodes_found`, which is misleading (for example, a permission error on `apt` is not "no nodes"). Catch `ResourceException` around the new per-node calls and return safe defaults (e.g., `version=None`, `updates=[]`) or map failures to a more accurate translation key.
