review_comment:
@lkostrowski It means that by, making a query by `App1`, I will be able to get details of `App2`. If you will check the `app` resolver, you will see, that we don't allow to fetch different app.
```
The authenticated app has access to its resources. Fetching different apps requires MANAGE_APPS permission.
```

But with your changes I can make request with `App1.token`, to get the access to the `app` owner details:
```graphql
{
	appExtension(id:"App2:Extension"){
		app{
			...
		}
	}
}
```
So to sum up, you're giving an access to something that wasn't allowed previously. Can you confirm that this is expected what you wanted to achieve?

