review_comment:
I would suggest to create the helper function for downloading the file, and second for processing oembed_data, then calling this inside this `else` section. 
```python
elif media_url:
    try:
        image = get_image()
        process_oembed_data(image)
    except ValidationError:
        ...
```
Right now there is a lot of things that happen here, we could make it more readable

Error messages/exceptions should never be returned, this can return sensitive information (especially in this instance, this could be used for probing networks):

```suggestion
                        raise ValidationError(
                            {
                                "media_url": ValidationError(
                                    f"Failed to fetch media file",
                                    code=ProductBulkCreateErrorCode.INVALID.value,
                                )
                            }
                        ) from exc
```

(this is CWE-209 https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/209.html if you are interesting to learn more about it)

Following the previous comment, we should make it clear we want a file object and not a path:

```suggestion
def validate_image_exif(image: IO[bytes]):

HTTP 3xx are also invalid (we are also missing the `400` status):
```suggestion
    if status_code < 200 or status_code >= 300:

First of all, for some records this resolver will return the value, but another record (like dismissed by user) will raise PermissionDenied. 
So while consuming the API, you need to have the implementation to cover the case when permission is raised. **Your app will not be able to fetch own problems, because one problem will be dismissed by Staff user.**

I think we could also make it more readable:

```python
if not root.dismissed:
    return None

# Return None, when you don't have access.
# Then you don't need to implement support for
#  catching the PermissionDenied errors on App side. 
if not has_permission:
    return None
elif root.dismissed_by_user_id:
    return UserByUserIdLoader
else:
    return AppByIdLoader()
```

`_validate_by_user_with_ids_input`, `_validate_by_user_with_keys_input`  and:

```python
if ids and len(ids) > MAX_ITEMS_LIMIT:
            raise ValidationError(
                {
                    "ids": ValidationError(
                        f"Cannot specify more than {MAX_ITEMS_LIMIT} IDs.",
                        code=AppProblemDismissErrorCodeEnum.INVALID.value,
                    )
                }
            )

        if keys and len(keys) > MAX_ITEMS_LIMIT:
            raise ValidationError(
                {
                    "keys": ValidationError(
                        f"Cannot specify more than {MAX_ITEMS_LIMIT} keys.",
                        code=AppProblemDismissErrorCodeEnum.INVALID.value,
                    )
                }
            )
```
from `_validate_by_app_input`.  Can be compressed to single method, that would accept: `field, field_name`. 
```python
def _validate_limit_for_field(cls, input_values: list[str], field_name:str) -> None:
    if len(input_values) > MAX_ITEMS_LIMIT:
        raise ValidationError(
                {
                    field_name: ValidationError(
                        f"Cannot specify more than {MAX_ITEMS_LIMIT}",
                        code=AppProblemDismissErrorCodeEnum.INVALID.value,
                    )
                }
            )
```

