Instead of iterating on each payment, I would propose to use `set`. Something like this (it is pseudo code):
```
    @classmethod
    def _check_payments_belong_to_order(cls, order, payments):
        order_payments = order.payments.filter(id__in=[p.id for p in payments])
        if set(order_payments) != set(payments):
            raise ValidationError(
                {
                    "payments_to_refund": ValidationError(
                        "These payments do not belong to the order.",
                        code=OrderErrorCode.PAYEMENTS_DO_NOT_BELONG_TO_ORDER,
                        params={"payments": get_nodes_or_error(set(payments).difference(set(order_payments)))},
                    )
                }
            )
```

