review_comment:
@AlanCoding I recommend using pathlib objects everywhere and only convert them to str when needed. But if you need a fixture that provides a string right away, you could have two fixtures — one depending on the other.

A backwards compatible example would look like this:
```python
@pytest.fixture
def private_data_dir_path(tmp_path: pathlib.Path) -> pathlib.Path:
   ...
   return <a pathlib object>

@pytest.fixture
def private_data_dir(private_data_dir_path: pathlib.Path) -> str:
   return str(private_data_dir_path)
```

