review_comment:
personally I don't think we need to explain how to use endpoints to its fullest, rather describe how to configure this particular endpoint + method.

for something concise:
"Create an instance group. Instances in this group determine an ordered preference for where a job will be executed"

```suggestion
    @extend_schema_if_available(extensions={"x-ai-description": "Cancel a running or pending workflow job"})
```

```suggestion
    @extend_schema_if_available(extensions={"x-ai-description": "Cancel a running or pending job."})
```

@fosterseth small correction, I don't think that statement is fully correct.

https://github.com/ansible/awx/blob/b34ee01fb34edbe3e4f26500ff5f4ccafb36c160/awx/main/models/ha.py#L414-L419

The instances in an instance group are unordered. The instance groups of some other resource are, but I agree, out of scope here. So you really don't want to say anything about preference ordering here, or else you'll imply something that it doesn't do.

