review_comment:
to give some history, the use of `psutil` here is completely ancient as of the original introduction https://github.com/ansible/awx/pull/2266

Then https://github.com/ansible/awx/pull/10954 changed to use the ansible-runner memory util. The issue of max_workers parity may not have really been on the radar at that point.

@kdelee did some work to fix basically this same problem in https://github.com/ansible/awx/pull/11800, but didn't touch the fact that psutil was used in a now one-off way.

@AlanCoding could you explain a little further what you mean by 

> Given that you don't need to pass it into finish_fact_cache, I'm also unclear if it should be passed into start_fact_cache. A semi-isolated way to do that might be to pass the full Inventory object from the outset.

Would you mind taking a look at what we have to see if it's good enough for this fix? I am happy to come up with a Jira to handle the additional refactoring if needed!

